  "instance_name": "mapping_001",
  "label": "The person is mapped as someone who is misinterpreting 'rocks' as marijuana",
  "description": "The text 'skip rocks, don't smoke them' implies that the person in the image is the one who is misinterpreting the word 'rocks' — likely thinking of marijuana instead of stones. The meme humorously projects the idea that the person is the one who is doing the 'wrong' thing (smoking rocks) instead of the 'right' thing (skipping rocks). The visual of the person skipping rocks is thus mapped onto the textual concept of someone who is confused or mistaken about what 'rocks' means, creating an analogical mapping where the person is the subject of the textual criticism.",
